A||||1||fieroboy||Suspension Mods||||5||
Z||000000||fieroboy||02-20-2000||03:29 PM||||I am thinking about putting coilovers front and rear on my 86 SE, but I am worried that it might make the ride to harsh. Can I get a spring rate that will be comfortable for daily driving?  Does the shock and strut you make a big difference?||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||02-20-2000||06:07 PM||||You can get just about any spring rate you want, from mushy to "shake the fillings out of your teeth" and everything thing in between. That's the beauty of coil-overs.  Yes, the type of shocks/struts you use can make a big difference. The choice are cheapy generic "no name" brands at the low end, to gas charged Monroes, KYBs, and Gabriels in the middle, to Bilsteins and Konis at the top end of the spectrum. The Koni's are adjustable and the ultimate in performance, but are very expensive too.||||reg||1
